<title>BRAZIL: Brazilian soybean and product basis levels.</title>
<headline>Brazilian soybean and product basis levels.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokers reported the</p>
<p>following Brazilian soybean and products basis levels.</p>
<p>(NS-no seller T-Trade P-Premium D-Discount NB-no bidder)</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	  BASIS	  MONTH	   PREVIOUS</p>
<p>Soybean (cents per bushel)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> August	    35/55 P	August	  40/50 P</p>
<p> Sept	    130/150 P	Sept	  140/150 P</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	  BASIS	  MONTH	   PREVIOUS</p>
<p>Soymeal/Pellets (dollars per short tonne 48 pct profat)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> August	    21/18 D	August	  22/19 D</p>
<p> Sept		2 D/4 P	Sept	    2 D/3 P</p>
<p> Oct		 16/18 P	Oct	     15/17 P</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	 BASIS	   MONTH	  PREVIOUS</p>
<p>Soybean Oil (dollars per tonne, points per lb, crude, degummed)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> August	   120/150 P	August	125/160 P</p>
<p> Sept	     110/160 P	Sept	  115/160 P</p>
<p> Oct		120/160 P	Oct	   130/160 P</p>
<p> Dec		100/150 P	Dec	     N/A</p>
</text>
